=head1 DESCRIPTION

The details of a user pool identity provider (IdP), including name and
type.

=head1 ATTRIBUTES


=head2 CreationDate => Str

The date and time when the item was created. Amazon Cognito returns
this timestamp in UNIX epoch time format. Your SDK might render the
output in a human-readable format like ISO 8601 or a Java C<Date>
object.


=head2 LastModifiedDate => Str

The date and time when the item was modified. Amazon Cognito returns
this timestamp in UNIX epoch time format. Your SDK might render the
output in a human-readable format like ISO 8601 or a Java C<Date>
object.


=head2 ProviderName => Str

The name of the IdP, for example C<MySAMLProvider>.


=head2 ProviderType => Str

The type of the provider, for example C<SAML>. Amazon Cognito supports
SAML 2.0, OIDC, and social IdPs. User pools list supported social IdPs
by name in this response parameter: Facebook, Google, Login with
Amazon, and Sign in with Apple.



